    <entry>
        <title>Dinemate Application Design</title>
        <author>
            <name>Maryam Moradi</name>
        </author>
        <link href="https://meeridesign.github.io/dinemate-application-design.html"/>
        <id>https://meeridesign.github.io/dinemate-application-design.html</id>
        <media:content url="https://meeridesign.github.io/media/posts/7/Psd-33x.jpg" medium="image" />
            <category term="UI/UX design"/>
            <category term="Typography"/>
            <category term="Logo design"/>
            <category term="Application design"/>

        <updated>2025-05-03T12:53:34+03:30</updated>
            <summary>
                <![CDATA[
                        <img src="https://meeridesign.github.io/media/posts/7/Psd-33x.jpg" alt="" />
                    The Problem Most existing restaurant-finder apps suffer from cluttered interfaces, weak search/filter&hellip;
                ]]>
            </summary>
        <content type="html">
            <![CDATA[
                    <p><img src="https://meeridesign.github.io/media/posts/7/Psd-33x.jpg" class="type:primaryImage" alt="" /></p>
                <h5 data-start="281" data-end="303"><strong data-start="286" data-end="301">The Problem</strong></h5>
<p class="" data-start="304" data-end="523">Most existing restaurant-finder apps suffer from cluttered interfaces, weak search/filter tools, and overly complex reservation processes. Users often abandon bookings due to confusing flows and lack of useful features.</p>
<h5 data-start="525" data-end="548"><strong data-start="530" data-end="546">Project Goal</strong></h5>
<p class="" data-start="549" data-end="715">Dinemate was designed to offer a clean, intuitive experience for discovering and reserving restaurants — with a focus on personalization, simplicity, and ease of use.</p>
<h5 data-start="717" data-end="743"><strong data-start="722" data-end="741">My Role &amp; Focus</strong></h5>
<ul data-start="744" data-end="992">
<li class="" data-start="744" data-end="837">
<p class="" data-start="746" data-end="837">Designed improved search and filtering for preferences like budget, cuisine, and location</p>
</li>
<li class="" data-start="744" data-end="837">
<p class="" data-start="746" data-end="837">Streamlined the reservation process for clarity and speed</p>
</li>
<li class="" data-start="900" data-end="992">
<p class="" data-start="902" data-end="992">Added features tailored to specific user needs, such as family dining or dietary filters</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h5 data-start="994" data-end="1028"><strong data-start="999" data-end="1026">Research &amp; Key Insights</strong></h5>
<p class="" data-start="1029" data-end="1077">User surveys revealed several recurring needs:</p>
<ul data-start="1078" data-end="1191">
<li class="" data-start="1078" data-end="1118">
<p class="" data-start="1080" data-end="1118">Interactive maps and table selection</p>
</li>
<li class="" data-start="1119" data-end="1151">
<p class="" data-start="1121" data-end="1151">Menu previews before booking</p>
</li>
<li class="" data-start="1152" data-end="1191">
<p class="" data-start="1154" data-end="1191">Child-friendly options for families</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="" data-start="1193" data-end="1312">These findings shaped a <strong data-start="1217" data-end="1231">user-first</strong> design approach and guided the app’s core functionality and interface decisions.</p>
<p data-start="1193" data-end="1312"> </p>
